{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Recorded the current account for the lost-commit receipt c7938884cd87410eb02432e32dc092ce (25 events, exit 0): comparison 0 is violated with a valid witness at parsed index 22 (the restarted former leader held one reconstructed voter against the three-voter entry at log index 106; control holds at 24) and comparison 2 is violated at the same index — its Apply completed (acknowledged, payload index 113) while the payload existed on exactly one of the three committed voters (payload_on_victims 0, durable_copies 1), the other two having reconstructed their own three-voter configuration and elected leadership without ever receiving it; the flag-disabled control acknowledged nothing at all (index 24). So a client-acknowledged decision rested on a minority of the committed configuration. Added a durability fact for that, extended the reconstruction fact to the three-voter ladder, kept the repair gap open and moved the discriminator to the unexecuted live-cluster repair question. Counterevidence recorded explicitly: the acknowledged copy was not discarded in the window (it stayed on the holder at index 113) and the new leadership formed in the same term as the stale leader, so the established failure is a single-copy acknowledgement, not an erased entry. Incomplete: the follower-repair probe (a restarted follower that stays in a cluster with a healthy leader) is not built yet.\"}"}}
